A||||6||GT Bastard||Anybody have experience with the Mayo Clinic in Minnesota?||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-15-2001||09:22 PM||||My mom is travelling there to get better medical treatment.  Nobody in her city has any idea what her condition is, and so she's heading there.  Is the Mayo Clinic just a really well-respected clinic, or is there something special about it?  Thanks for any info...||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||03-15-2001||09:59 PM||||according to my fiance', Melinda, it is a very well respected and advanced clinic.  they have a lot of advanced techniques and equipment.  they are able to do things that most other facilities can't.  i guess it's kinda like going to Duke Medical center, here in the South.<P>both her grandmother and mother have been there for various ailments.  her grandmother needed hip replacement surgury, but she had emphazima, so know one but Mayo would operate on her.  <P>hope that helps, somewhat.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||03-15-2001||11:25 PM||||I get reports periodically on some of my patients that go up there.  They do a great job, especially if someone has something unusual.  But they handle the run-of-the-mill problems well, too.  I would say that in the midwest it is the place to go.<P>In our country we in 2001 have MANY outstanding medical facilities besides Mayo that are equally as good, but geographically Mayo makes the most sense for her.<P>Just tell her to brace herself for a whirlwind of activity, because likely they will do TONS of tests.  That's how they operate, which is appropriate if someone is having trouble getting a diagnosis.  Just hope she has good insurance.<P>I wish her the best.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jimmy||03-15-2001||11:54 PM||||     They are one of the best.  I have a friend who dislocated her shoulder which pinched a nerve in her arm, leaving her arm/hand with no feeling.   The hospitals in MPLS redislocated her shoulder SIX times and did many tests but could not get the feeling back in her arm.  They said she was going to have to live with it.  It seemed nobody was able to help her out.  However, ther was one doctor who did reccomend a specialist at the Mayo clinic.  Almost a half a year later the Mayo clinic was able to go in and operate on her shoulder.  She now has 90%-95% of her feeling back in her arm/hand.  This is just one of many cases I know of people getting the help they could not find anywhere else.  Also many people from out of the country are sent to the Mayo clinic.  Ther was some King from an Arab Nation that was residing at the Clinic for treatment about a year ago.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||03-15-2001||11:54 PM||||A guy that sits next to me at work just made a trip there about a month or so ago.  From what he's told me, it's a great place to go for treatment.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||03-16-2001||12:35 AM||||I don't have any direct experience unless you count driving past it. I don't recall EVER hearing or reading a negative comment about their abilities though. Downright amazing reputation...||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||03-16-2001||08:22 AM||||Cool, thanks for all the info guys!||||reg||1
